{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>האכלתם</b> — Rabbi Moses said: in place of bread, tears." "<b>ותשקמו דמעות שליש</b> — Invert it: ותשקמו דמעות בשליש, and it is a measure, like וכל בשליש. And it is possible that this is a figurative way, for their food and their drink are tears." "<b>And the bet in דמעות</b> — like לכו לחמו בלחמי ושתו ביין מסכתי, or the bet in דמעות serves another function: ותשקמו דמעות, or בדמעות — the meaning is the same, whether with a bet or without one. And so it is: האכלתם לחם דמעה — and according to any interpretation, the meaning is Israel in exile."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {2 "The phrase 'הטעם שוה בשליש או תחסר אות בי\"ת' is ambiguous; read hyper-literally as 'the meaning is the same, with a shalish or missing the letter bet.' It is unclear whether 'בשליש' refers to the word שליש from the verse or means 'in a third [interpretation].' Translated as 'with a bet or without one' following the context of the preceding alternatives."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:34.412740558Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}